{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795426304,"nonce":"pHaNdqSX/sDukt6V2fSbRdk6tyU=","title":"JAX 0.10.1: a second traced window march is called with one input buffer short","message":"Found on feat/fvm. FVMParticipant.march compiled one window program per CFL substep count. When the count changed, the second traced program (gas receiving interface data through _override) ran its first call and failed on the second: Execution supplied 28 buffers but compiled program expected 29 (AOT: Computation compiled for 29 inputs but called with 28; const_args 26 + 2 inputs). jax.clear_caches() before it avoided it. Worked around by deciding the substeps inside the program (one program for every window, timeschemes._cfl_substeps). Not reduced to a JAX reproducer.","files":null}]}